WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:16.112
Julia cried as Heracles disappeared.

2
00:00:17.153 --> 00:00:20.156
She leaped forward and grabbed at the temple wall with her fingers.

3
00:00:21.116 --> 00:00:23.679
But there was nothing there except solid stone.

4
00:00:24.279 --> 00:00:26.661
The rift had disappeared too.

5
00:00:28.142 --> 00:00:32.345
She sank onto the floor, hardly believing what had just happened.

6
00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:34.606
Heracles was gone.

7
00:00:35.526 --> 00:00:39.928
And now Julia and Brody were trapped in ancient Greece forever!

8
00:00:41.129 --> 00:00:42.510
Brody looked stunned too.

9
00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:47.132
"I can't believe that just happened," he murmured.

10
00:00:48.292 --> 00:00:50.733
Julia saw him staring at the wall behind her.

11
00:00:50.753 --> 00:00:53.034
"Whoa!" he cried.

12
00:00:53.054 --> 00:00:54.535
"What's going on?"

13
00:00:56.095 --> 00:00:56.936
Julia looked up.

14
00:00:57.896 --> 00:01:01.137
A faint spark of light was coming through a tiny crack in the wall.

15
00:01:02.558 --> 00:01:05.479
She stood and backed away, not daring to hope.

16
00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.621
Then a hand pushed through the wall, and another.

17
00:01:10.741 --> 00:01:11.722
Julia gasped.

18
00:01:12.162 --> 00:01:14.143
"Heracles!" she cried.

19
00:01:15.343 --> 00:01:19.805
They all stared at the wall in disbelief as the hands struggled to push the wall apart.

20
00:01:20.845 --> 00:01:23.487
Julia could hear Heracles grunting with effort.

21
00:01:24.807 --> 00:01:25.627
"He's doing it!"

22
00:01:25.888 --> 00:01:26.708
Brody shouted.

23
00:01:27.424 --> 00:01:29.146
"He's opening the rift back up!"

24
00:01:30.747 --> 00:01:33.489
"Impossible!" Hera moaned.

25
00:01:36.151 --> 00:01:37.632
It did seem impossible.

26
00:01:38.653 --> 00:01:44.678
But sure enough, Heracles was prying open the time passage that had just closed behind him!

27
00:01:45.819 --> 00:01:50.002
Soon the rift was wide enough for Heracles to wedge his upper body into it.

28
00:01:51.223 --> 00:01:53.485
Brody just stood there, staring in amazement.

29
00:01:53.505 --> 00:01:55.947
"Brody, help him!"

30
00:01:56.347 --> 00:01:57.088
Julia cried.

31
00:01:58.048 --> 00:01:59.308
"We have to get him through!"

32
00:02:01.049 --> 00:02:03.930
She grabbed Heracles' hand and pulled as hard as she could.

33
00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:06.590
For a moment nothing happened.

34
00:02:07.731 --> 00:02:10.231
Then Brody grabbed the hero's other hand.

35
00:02:11.192 --> 00:02:15.153
Heracles grimaced with pain as his broad shoulders scraped against the wall.

36
00:02:15.173 --> 00:02:17.833
"Don't pull me all the way through yet."

37
00:02:18.254 --> 00:02:19.594
He gasped out the words.

38
00:02:19.614 --> 00:02:24.375
"You have to get through the passage before it closes again!"

39
00:02:25.135 --> 00:02:26.596
Julia realized he was right.

40
00:02:27.704 --> 00:02:30.026
"But how can we fit through while you're in there too?"

41
00:02:30.466 --> 00:02:31.066
she asked.

42
00:02:32.187 --> 00:02:41.293
"Just give me a moment Heracles grunted and groaned, flexing the muscles in his powerful legs.

43
00:02:42.354 --> 00:02:45.956
He spread his legs apart, pushing the walls farther to the sides.

44
00:02:46.977 --> 00:02:51.800
Soon there was enough space—barely—for a person to duck between his legs.

45
00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:54.222
"Come on, Brody!"

46
00:02:54.622 --> 00:02:55.443
Julia cried.

47
00:02:55.463 --> 00:02:59.669
"Hurry," Heracles said through gritted teeth.

48
00:02:59.689 --> 00:03:06.293
"I don't know how much longer I can hold it open."

49
00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:08.174
"Thank you!"

50
00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:11.896
Julia cried, diving for the opening between Heracles' feet.

51
00:03:11.916 --> 00:03:14.077
"Thank you so much!"

52
00:03:14.977 --> 00:03:18.159
Brody still looked confused, so Julia grabbed his hand.

53
00:03:19.239 --> 00:03:23.602
She pulled him after her through Heracles' legs—and through the rift.

54
00:03:24.482 --> 00:03:27.444
Behind them, Julia heard Hera ranting.

55
00:03:28.528 --> 00:03:31.090
"You'll pay for defying me, Heracles!"

56
00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:32.271
she screamed.

57
00:03:33.752 --> 00:03:41.937
"Trust me, you won't have an easy day for the rest of your life, mark my Snap!

58
00:03:42.297 --> 00:03:46.060
Julia tumbled out of the rift onto the sidewalk near the school gym.

59
00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:50.283
"Ow," she said as her elbow scraped the pavement.

60
00:03:51.483 --> 00:03:53.645
Brody was lying on the ground beside her.

61
00:03:54.506 --> 00:03:57.908
He sat up and looked at the brick wall of the school building.

62
00:03:58.640 --> 00:03:59.621
Julia looked too.

63
00:04:00.761 --> 00:04:04.142
The wall appeared normal, with no sign of the rift.

64
00:04:05.463 --> 00:04:07.104
She stood up and gazed around.

65
00:04:08.024 --> 00:04:10.945
Actually, everything looked normal.

66
00:04:12.086 --> 00:04:14.247
Brody looked at Julia and grinned.

67
00:04:14.267 --> 00:04:17.668
"I guess we're not in ancient Greece anymore."

68
00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:26.452
A few days later, Julia pushed open the door to the school library and went inside.

69
00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:30.922
She had a math test the next day, and she needed to study.

70
00:04:32.043 --> 00:04:36.306
As she passed a table, she saw a copy of the school newspaper lying there.

71
00:04:37.367 --> 00:04:41.470
She picked it up, glancing at the photograph of Brody on the front page.

72
00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:45.552
Below the picture was the article she'd written about him.

73
00:04:45.572 --> 00:04:49.315
"Yo," a familiar voice said behind her.

74
00:04:49.335 --> 00:04:52.437
"Admiring your greatest article ever, huh?"

75
00:04:55.539 --> 00:04:56.520
Julia looked up.

76
00:04:57.436 --> 00:04:59.218
Brody stood there, grinning at her.

77
00:05:00.018 --> 00:05:02.100
A book was tucked under his arm.

78
00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:04.562
"What are you doing here?"

79
00:05:05.043 --> 00:05:05.623
she asked.

80
00:05:05.643 --> 00:05:09.006
"I didn't think you even knew where the library was!"

81
00:05:09.026 --> 00:05:11.969
"Ha-ha!" Brody laughed.

82
00:05:12.669 --> 00:05:13.110
"Good one!"

83
00:05:14.251 --> 00:05:15.972
Then he held up the book to show her.

84
00:05:16.673 --> 00:05:18.234
It was about ancient Greece.

85
00:05:19.355 --> 00:05:20.676
Julia raised an eyebrow.

86
00:05:21.897 --> 00:05:24.820
She looked around to make sure nobody was close enough to hear them.

87
00:05:26.048 --> 00:05:28.750
"Don't you know enough about that topic already?"

88
00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:30.731
Brody shrugged.

89
00:05:30.751 --> 00:05:33.652
"You can always learn more about stuff, right?

90
00:05:34.933 --> 00:05:37.335
Anyway, some of those myths you told me were interesting."

91
00:05:38.195 --> 00:05:40.016
He stuck the book in his backpack.

92
00:05:40.036 --> 00:05:44.759
"And I want to find out more about what happens to Heracles later."

93
00:05:45.879 --> 00:05:46.720
Julia nodded.

94
00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:50.142
She couldn't stop thinking about Heracles herself.

95
00:05:51.563 --> 00:05:56.329
He was going to have a hard time with Hera; Julia knew that from the myths she'd read.

96
00:05:57.329 --> 00:05:59.890
Had Julia and Brody made things even worse for him?

97
00:06:00.871 --> 00:06:01.631
She hoped not.

98
00:06:02.411 --> 00:06:05.053
But she supposed they'd never find out for sure.

99
00:06:05.073 --> 00:06:10.595
"We've only been back for a few days, but it seems like longer, doesn't it?"

100
00:06:11.055 --> 00:06:11.495
she said.

101
00:06:11.515 --> 00:06:14.416
"Sort of," Brody replied.

102
00:06:14.436 --> 00:06:18.038
"It's weird how no time passed while we were gone."

103
00:06:19.238 --> 00:06:20.399
Julia nodded again.

104
00:06:21.459 --> 00:06:26.574
When they'd returned through the rift, she and Brody had quickly figured out that only a few seconds

105
00:06:26.634 --> 00:06:28.816
had passed in their time while they were away.

106
00:06:31.258 --> 00:06:35.461
That was definitely strange, because they'd been in ancient Greece for a couple of weeks.

107
00:06:36.722 --> 00:06:40.064
So many things had happened to the two of them during those weeks!

108
00:06:41.285 --> 00:06:45.348
But now that they were back in their own time, it was as if nothing had changed.

109
00:06:46.909 --> 00:06:47.509
She shrugged.

110
00:06:47.529 --> 00:06:49.991
"I guess that's how time travel works.

111
00:06:50.571 --> 00:06:51.072
Who knew?"

112
00:06:52.196 --> 00:06:55.738
Just then several popular kids came into the library.

113
00:06:57.518 --> 00:06:59.099
They spotted Brody and waved.

114
00:07:00.239 --> 00:07:03.341
Suddenly one of the girls noticed Julia standing there.

115
00:07:03.361 --> 00:07:05.181
"Hi, Julia!"

116
00:07:05.682 --> 00:07:06.922
she said, hurrying over.

117
00:07:06.942 --> 00:07:12.384
"I've been meaning to tell you, I really like your article about Brody."

118
00:07:12.404 --> 00:07:15.525
"Thanks," Julia said shyly.

119
00:07:15.545 --> 00:07:19.227
"Julia?" The other girl hurried over too.

120
00:07:19.247 --> 00:07:21.628
"I'm having a party this weekend.

121
00:07:22.836 --> 00:07:24.117
It's Saturday night at eight.

122
00:07:24.837 --> 00:07:25.998
I hope you can come."

123
00:07:26.018 --> 00:07:29.801
"Yeah, Julia, you should go," Brody put in.

124
00:07:29.821 --> 00:07:31.021
"I'll be there."

125
00:07:31.041 --> 00:07:34.103
"Thanks," Julia said.

126
00:07:34.123 --> 00:07:38.346
"I um I think I can probably make it."

127
00:07:38.366 --> 00:07:41.348
"Great!" The girl smiled.

128
00:07:42.769 --> 00:07:45.650
Julia was smiling too as the girls walked away.

129
00:07:47.011 --> 00:07:47.752
She was wrong.

130
00:07:49.125 --> 00:07:53.463
Some things had changed since she and Brody traveled to ancient Greece!
